USAGE
  typepeek overview [--access import|require] [--workspace path] [--json] [--pretty] [--match substring] [--subpaths] <specifier>
  typepeek export [--access import|require] [--workspace path] [--json] [--pretty] <specifier> <export-name>
  typepeek signatures [--access import|require] [--workspace path] [--json] [--pretty] <specifier> <export-name>
  typepeek plan [--access import|require] [--workspace path] [--json] [--pretty] <specifier> <queries-json>
  typepeek search [--access import|require] [--workspace path] [--json] [--pretty] <specifier> <query>
  typepeek subpaths [--access import|require] [--workspace path] [--json] [--pretty] <specifier>
  typepeek declarations [--access import|require] [--workspace path] [--json] [--pretty] <specifier> <export-name>
  typepeek member [--access import|require] [--workspace path] [--json] [--pretty] <specifier> <export-name> <member-path>
  typepeek members [--access import|require] [--workspace path] [--json] [--pretty] [--match substring] <specifier> <export-name> [<member-path>]
  typepeek compare [--before-access import|require] [--after-access import|require] [--before-workspace path] [--after-workspace path] [--json] [--pretty] <before-specifier> <after-specifier>
  typepeek capabilities [--json] [--pretty]
  typepeek protocol
  typepeek --help
  typepeek --version

Start with overview to discover exports. Use search or subpaths for lighter discovery; members to discover public members; declarations or member for narrow declaration questions; signatures for parameters; export for declarations and Supporting Types; plan to share one evidence snapshot; and compare to diff two overview indexes. Agents can run capabilities before invoking protocol through bounded stdin/stdout. Common flags may precede or follow an explicit inspection command.

FLAGS
  -h --help     Print help information and exit
  -v --version  Print version information and exit
     --         All subsequent inputs should be interpreted as arguments

COMMANDS
  overview      Index the Module Exports and Public Subpaths of one Inspectable Module.
  export        Inspect one Module Export with declarations and bounded Supporting Types.
  signatures    Inspect only the public call and construct signatures of one Module Export.
  plan          Execute a bounded query list over one shared Installed Evidence snapshot.
  search        Search the bounded Module Export index without returning an overview.
  subpaths      Discover manifest Public Subpaths without materializing a TypeScript program.
  declarations  Inspect only the declarations of one Module Export.
  member        Inspect exactly one public Member path of a Module Export.
  members       Discover immediate public Members and their declaration spaces.
  compare       Compare two complete Interface Overview indexes without merging variants.
  capabilities  Print the Inspection Core capabilities as JSON.
  protocol      Invoke the Inspection Protocol with one bounded JSON request on stdin.
